# gsap-timeline

- `gsap.timeline()` for any multi-step animation. Avoid chained `delay`.
- Position parameter: numeric (`0.5`), absolute label (`"start"`), relative (`"+=0.3"`, `"-=0.2"`), previous-tween-relative (`"<"`, `"<0.1"`, `">"`).
- Labels via `.addLabel("name", time)`; reference with `"name+=0.2"`.
- Nest timelines: `parent.add(childTimeline, "label")` — child plays in parent's coordinate space.
- `defaults: { ease: "expo.out", duration: 0.4 }` on the master timeline so every child inherits unless overridden.

For full reference: `skills/gsap-timeline/SKILL.md`.
